.TH "COMPLYCTL\-PROVIDER\-AMPEL" "1" "September 2026" "ComplyTime Manual"
.SH NAME
complyctl\-provider\-ampel \- Ampel scanning provider for complyctl
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]complyctl\-provider\-ampel\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]complyctl\-provider\-ampel\f[R] is a gRPC plugin for
\f[B]complyctl\f[R](1) that provides compliance scanning capabilities
using the Ampel evaluation engine.
It is not invoked directly by users; \f[B]complyctl\f[R] discovers and
launches it automatically when the provider is installed.
.PP
The provider receives assessment configurations from \f[B]complyctl\f[R]
and evaluates repository configurations against granular security
policies (e.g., branch protection rules) using the \f[B]snappy\f[R] and
\f[B]ampel\f[R] CLI tools.
Results include per\-tenet messages and remediation guidance.
.PP
Communication with \f[B]complyctl\f[R] uses the hashicorp/go\-plugin
gRPC interface, implementing three RPCs: \f[B]Describe\f[R],
\f[B]Generate\f[R], and \f[B]Scan\f[R].
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is provided through variables defined in assessment plan
targets.
These variables are passed to the provider via \f[B]complyctl\f[R] and
are not set manually by the user.
.TP
\f[B]url\f[R] (required)
HTTPS URL of the repository to scan.
Must use the HTTPS scheme.
Example: \f[B]https://github.com/org/repo\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]specs\f[R] (required)
Comma\-separated list of spec references identifying the policy files to
evaluate.
Example: \f[B]builtin:github/branch\-rules.yaml\f[R].
Path traversal sequences (\f[B]../\f[R]) are rejected.
.TP
\f[B]branches\f[R] (optional)
Comma\-separated list of branches to scan.
Must match the pattern \f[B][a\-zA\-Z0\-9._/\-]+\f[R].
Path traversal sequences are rejected.
Default: \f[B]main\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]access_token\f[R] (optional)
Authentication token for accessing private repositories.
Rejected if it contains newlines or null bytes.
.TP
\f[B]platform\f[R] (optional)
Platform hint for self\-hosted instances (e.g., \f[B]github\f[R],
\f[B]gitlab\f[R]).
Used when hostname\-based detection fails to identify the platform.
Default: auto\-detected from the URL hostname.
.TP
\f[B]ampel_policy_dir\f[R] (optional, global variable)
Custom directory containing granular Ampel policy source files.
Takes second priority after complypack content.
Default: \f[B].complytime/ampel/granular\-policies/\f[R]
.SH ENVIRONMENT
No environment variables are read directly by this provider.
.SH EXTERNAL TOOLS
Requires \f[B]snappy\f[R] and \f[B]ampel\f[R] CLI tools at runtime.
These tools are not currently packaged in Fedora and must be installed
separately.
See the Carabiner project for installation instructions: \c
.UR https://github.com/carabiner-dev
.UE \c
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I].complytime/ampel/\f[R]
Provider workspace directory.
All paths below are relative to the current working directory.
.TP
\f[I].complytime/ampel/results/<repo>\-<branch>\-<spec>\-snappy.intoto.json\f[R]
In\-toto attestation produced by \f[B]snappy snap\f[R].
Contains raw API data collected from the repository (e.g., branch
protection rules).
The filename encodes the sanitized repository URL, branch, and spec
label.
.TP
\f[I].complytime/ampel/results/<repo>\-<branch>\-<spec>\-ampel.intoto.json\f[R]
In\-toto attestation produced by \f[B]ampel verify\f[R].
Contains the policy evaluation results against the snappy\-collected
data.
The filename follows the same pattern as the snappy attestation.
.TP
\f[I].complytime/ampel/results/<repo>\-<branch>.json\f[R]
Per\-repository result JSON summarizing findings for a single repository
and branch combination.
.TP
\f[I].complytime/ampel/policy/scan\-config.json\f[R]
Scan configuration written by the \f[B]Generate\f[R] RPC.
Records the matched requirement IDs so the \f[B]Scan\f[R] RPC can
synthesize passing assessments for requirements with no findings.
.TP
\f[I].complytime/ampel/policy/\f[R]
Merged AMPEL policy bundle generated from granular policy files.
.TP
\f[I].complytime/ampel/granular\-policies/\f[R]
Default directory for granular AMPEL policy source files.
Overridden by \f[B]ampel_policy_dir\f[R] or complypack content.
.SH EVIDENCE
The provider records \f[B]Evidence\f[R] entries on each
\f[B]AssessmentLog\f[R] returned by the \f[B]Scan\f[R] RPC.
Two attestation types are produced per repository/branch/spec
combination:
.TP
\f[B]Snappy attestation\f[R] (type: \f[B]IntotoAttestation\f[R])
The \f[B]snappy\f[R] tool collects raw API data from the repository
platform (e.g., GitHub branch protection settings) and produces an
in\-toto attestation.
This attestation captures the observed state of the repository at scan
time.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Source.Coordinate\f[R]: path to the snappy attestation file
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Source.Digest\f[R]: \f[B]sha256:<hex>\f[R] digest of the
attestation file
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Source.ReferenceID\f[R]: \f[B]snappy\-<spec\-label>\f[R]
.RE
.TP
\f[B]Ampel attestation\f[R] (type: \f[B]IntotoAttestation\f[R])
The \f[B]ampel\f[R] tool evaluates granular security policies against
the snappy\-collected data and produces an in\-toto attestation
containing the evaluation results.
A non\-zero exit code indicates policy failures, not tool errors.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Source.Coordinate\f[R]: path to the ampel result attestation file
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Source.Digest\f[R]: \f[B]sha256:<hex>\f[R] digest of the
attestation file
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Source.ReferenceID\f[R]: \f[B]ampel\-<spec\-label>\f[R]
.RE
.SH EXIT CODES
This provider is a gRPC subprocess managed by \f[B]complyctl\f[R].
Exit codes follow the hashicorp/go\-plugin protocol and are not
user\-facing.
